\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Establish the general Arthur-Langlands reciprocity correspondence between constituents of the discrete automorphic spectrum of a connected reductive group $G$ and the appropriate global Galois or Arthur parameters, compatibly with localization and automorphic $L$-functions.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2024/54}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Establish the general Arthur-Langlands reciprocity correspondence between constituents of the discrete automorphic spectrum of a connected reductive group $G$ and the appropriate global Galois or Arthur parameters, compatibly with localization and automorphic $L$-functions.

